#question(title: [Implicit differentiation])[
  The equation
  $
    sin(x + y) + x y^2 = 0
  $
  defines a function $display(y = h(x))$ near
  $(0, 0)$.
  #link("https://www.desmos.com/calculator/bvupq00r6s")[#goto-button[graph]]

  Using implicit differentiation, compute
  #grid(
    columns: 4,
    column-gutter: 1em,
    [
      + $display(h(0))$
    ],
    [
      2. $display(h' (0))$
    ],
    [
      3. $display(h^(' ') (0))$
    ],
    [
      4. $display(h^(' ' ') (0))$
    ],
  )
]
